<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="commercekings_app_health" translate="label" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
            <label>App health</label>
            <tab>commercekings</tab>
            <resource>CommerceKings_AppHealth::config</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label comment" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Alerts</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Checks Magento every 5 minutes and tells you on a change: a problem, then "Resolved". An hourly status proves that alerts can go out.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\Enabled</backend_model>
                    <comment>On: the checks run and messages are sent. All App health settings are global (default scope).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="domain" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="15" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Shop domain</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\Domain</frontend_model>
                    <comment>App health stays silent on a copy of this shop (staging, a developer's database).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="channel" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Channel</label>
                    <comment>A Notification channel that sends text, e.g. slack (with module-notification-slack). Slack gets formatted messages, another text channel plain text. Not email: it sends templates.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="recipient" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Recipient</label>
                    <comment>Where the global messages go, in the channel's format, e.g. for slack a Slack channel ID (C0123456789, at the bottom of the channel's details).</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="website_channels" translate="label comment" sortOrder="35" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Website channels</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\WebsiteChannels</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\WebsiteChannels</backend_model>
                    <comment>A website's own messages (its email settings, unsent sales emails, its daily summary) to its own channel. Without a row: the global channel.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="shared_to_websites" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="36" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Also post shared problems to website channels</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>The shared checks' alerts (cron, logs, queues, ...) also to each website channel. Security findings stay global. Default: No.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="summary" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Daily summary</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>One global summary, and one per website channel with that website's own items.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="summary_time" translate="label comment" type="time" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Daily summary at</label>
                    <comment>In the default store's time zone; a website channel's summary in the website's.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field><field id="summary">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="repeat_hours" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Repeat a failing check after (hours)</label>
                    <comment>A check still failing is sent again after this long. Default: 6.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="recover_runs" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="61" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Resolved after (OK runs in a row)</label>
                    <comment>Window checks (logs, queues, sending) resolve after this many OK runs in a row. Default: 2.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="notice_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="62" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>New log errors at most every (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>New critical log errors and security findings: at most one message per check this often; the rest goes in the next. Default: 30.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="hourly_status" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="63" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Hourly status</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>A status every hour through the alerts' queue: posted when something is not OK, and once a day as "All checks OK". More: README &gt; When you hear about what.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="hourly_status_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="64" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Hourly status every (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 60; 15 to 180.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-number-range number-range-15-180</validate>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\HourlyMinutes</backend_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field><field id="hourly_status">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="include_log_message" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="65" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Add the masked log message</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Default: No - only the error's type, count, time and file:line leave the server. Yes: also a masked one-line message (emails, phones, numbers, tokens and secrets hidden; names and free text may show).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="heartbeat_url" translate="label comment" type="obscure" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Heartbeat URL</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <comment>An uptime service's heartbeat URL (e.g. Healthchecks.io), pinged every 5 minutes while alerts can go out. Stored encrypted. More: README &gt; Before going live.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="test" translate="label comment" type="button" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Test</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\TestAlert</frontend_model>
                    <comment>Sends one message now to the saved global channel and recipient. Save first.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="status_now" translate="label comment" type="button" sortOrder="85" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Status</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\StatusNow</frontend_model>
                    <comment>Runs the checks now and posts the result to the global recipient: problems, warnings, what is not set up, recent log errors. Alerts and the hourly status keep their timing.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="cron" translate="label comment" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Cron</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>No job has run, a job runs too long, or jobs end with an error.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="stale_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>No job has run for (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 5.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="running_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>A job running for over (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 60.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="quiet_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>A failing job counts as fixed after (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>A failing job stays failing until it runs OK, or this long without an error. Default: 60.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="indexers" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Indexers</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>An indexer invalid, or stuck working.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>For over (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 60.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="caches" translate="label comment" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Caches</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>A cache type disabled (at once), or invalidated and not refreshed.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Invalidated for over (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 60.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="maintenance" translate="label comment" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Maintenance mode</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Maintenance mode left on.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>On for over (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 15.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="system_log" translate="label comment" sortOrder="55" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>System log</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>New errors in var/log/system.log (and extra files): critical ones at once, errors in the hourly status, spikes. More: README &gt; What is checked.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="error_count" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Alert at (errors)</label>
                    <comment>ERROR and above. Default: 20.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="window_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Within (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 5.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="max_read_kb" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Read at most (KB per run and file)</label>
                    <comment>Of a larger backlog only the newest part is read (counts then "at least"). Default: 1024.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="file" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Log file</label>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\LogFile</backend_model>
                    <comment>A file in var/log. Default: system.log.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="extra_files" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="90" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Extra log files</label>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\LogFiles</backend_model>
                    <comment>More var/log files in the same format, one per line (e.g. payment.log), at most 5; never debug.log.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="immediate_files" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="95" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Errors at once from</label>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\ImmediateLogFiles</backend_model>
                    <comment>ERROR entries of these files are sent at once (like CRITICAL), not in the hourly status: system.log, exception.log or Extra log files. Default: none.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="sensitive_data" translate="label comment" sortOrder="58" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Sensitive data in logs</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Card numbers, secrets and personal data written into logs: a security alert at once, to the global channel only, never the value. More: README &gt; Sensitive data in logs.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="rule_settings" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Rule settings</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\RuleSettings</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\SensitiveRules</backend_model>
                    <comment>Turn a rule set or a rule off or on, or give it another severity: e.g. "personal" 0, or "pci/card_cvv" with warning. Codes: README.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="custom_rules" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Custom rules</label>
                    <frontend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\CustomRules</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\SensitiveRules</backend_model>
                    <comment>Regex rules of your own, in a shipped rule set or a new one; checked on save. More: README &gt; Sensitive data in logs.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="exceptions" translate="label comment" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Exceptions</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>New entries in var/log/exception.log: a new exception at once, and spikes with the top classes.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="count" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Alert at (entries)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 20.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="window_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Within (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 15.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="max_read_kb" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Read at most (KB per run)</label>
                    <comment>Of a larger backlog only the newest part is read (counts then "at least"). Default: 1024.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="file" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Log file</label>
                    <backend_model>CommerceKings\AppHealth\Model\Config\Backend\LogFile</backend_model>
                    <comment>A file in var/log. Default: exception.log.</comment>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="queues" translate="label comment" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Queues</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Message queue backlogs (RabbitMQ or MySQL queue), counts only. Off by default: it connects to the broker every run.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="max_messages" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Alert at (messages in a queue)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 1000.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="growing_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Or growing for (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 15.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="email_failing" translate="label comment" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Mail delivery errors</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Mail transport errors in the logs, and failing CommerceKings notifications.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="failed_reminders" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Alert at (failing notifications)</label>
                    <comment>Failed in the last hour, e.g. cart reminders. Default: 3.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="quiet_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Mail counts as working again after (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>After a mail error it stays failing until a mail goes out, or this long without an error. Default: 60.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="email_disabled" translate="label comment" sortOrder="90" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Email communications disabled</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Disable Email Communications set to Yes for a website's store views. Reported per website; see Website channels.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="sales_emails" translate="label comment" sortOrder="100" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Unsent sales emails</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>Sales emails not sent in time (the last 24 hours; cancelled and closed orders left out). Reported per website; see Website channels.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="unsent_count" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Alert at (unsent emails)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 3.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="unsent_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Unsent after (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 30.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="external" translate="label comment" sortOrder="110" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Server status</label>
                <fieldset_css>commercekings-config-section</fieldset_css>
                <comment>What your servers report (containers, disk, services, ...): failing lines, and servers that stop reporting. More: README &gt; System status from your server.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="stale_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>No status for (minutes)</label>
                    <comment>A server that reported before and is silent this long is a problem. Default: 15.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
